WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:02.635
-Our first guest
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:06.238
and comedian who is hosting
the MTV Movie and TV Awards

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.241
this Sunday at 9:00 p.m.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.943
Please welcome, Leslie Jones!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.446
Leslie!
Aha-ha!

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:18.251
Leslie!
Come on, now. Aww!

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.253
Leslie, thank you so much
for coming back to the show.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:22.789
It's always good
to see you, bud.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:25.624
-Yes, baby, I love you!
What's up?!

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:30.162
-Thank you, thank you.
Now, I follow you on Twitter,

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:31.897
and I see all the stuff you do.

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:35.401
I saw that you got your vaccine,
so congratulations on that.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:38.171
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.473
You filmed the whole process
and everything.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.007
That was very cool
that you did that.

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:43.976
You admitted that you were
nervous going in.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:46.679
How did it compare
to what you expected?

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.249
-It was actually way easier.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:52.519
I think it's good to give
yourself a very nice

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:56.823
paranoid fear,
so then when it turns out

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.291
less than what it is,
then you're good.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.794
-Yeah.
-So, I was scared.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.664
I honestly had planned
on not even taking it.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.532
I'mma be honest, I was kind of
one of those people

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.335
that was like, "Nah,
this doesn't sound like

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.471
the right thing to do,"
but my aunt --

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.840
my aunt is
a drug enforcement agent.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.910
And she put me on the phone
with a biologist.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.246
And they was like,
"Nah, you gonna do this."

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.715
[ Laughter ]
-All right, good. I'm glad!

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.751
Good, I'm so happy.
And you look fantastic,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.386
so good, good, good.
-Thank you.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:29.155
-By the way, I love your
Uber Eats commercials.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.423
Is that the one where
you're acting with yourself?

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.758
-Oh!
Yes, I love those.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.261
Those were so fun.
-Dude, you're a good co-star

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.296
with yourself.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:40.366
-I mean, I do love myself.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.369
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.305
We talked in the past about how
I love when you live tweet.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:48.841
When you live tweet anything,
it always makes me laugh,

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.243
and most recently,
you live-tweeted

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:53.846
Zack Snyder's cut
of "Justice League"

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:57.650
with the hashtag --
-The best -- the best version!

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.386
Thank you!
The best cut of that movie!

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.420
Thank you!

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.756
-But you did the hashtag
#longassmovie.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.059
Did you know
it's four hours long?

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.194
I haven't seen it yet,
but Nancy, my wife,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.596
saw it, loved it.
But it was great?

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:14.000
-I knew it was four hours.
I was amazed that I was gonna

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.270
get to sit down
and watch four hours

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.372
of Wonder Woman and Batman.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.840
I was so excited.
I was excited.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.144
So I just I timed myself, like,
"I'm 30 minutes in!

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:28.381
I got 3 hours and 44 seconds
left!"

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.916
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:34.487
-We actually put together
highlights of your commentary

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:37.756
while watching "Justice League."
Take a look at this.

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:41.094
-That's so dope!
Uggh, bitch!

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.662
That's good.
No, it's good.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.764
I just blew out the whole side
of this building

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.832
that y'all been
going to school here for years.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.835
You mean to tell me everybody
else under the water

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.437
got armor on,
but he got skinny jeans on?

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:56.342
Oh, he mad, fighting all
the arms coming out -- ow!

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.244
Who is he?!

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.612
See, it always come down
to somebody trying

00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:02.415
to make they daddy happy!

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.817
Go to therapy!

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:09.021
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
-Dude, come on!

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:11.190
It was so --
[ Laughs ]

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.893
It was so worth sitting through,
because Zack Snyder himself

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.161
gave you a shout-out.
Look at this.

00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:17.997
He said --
-Yasss!

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.432
-Look at this,
"The official ZSJL whisperer.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.567
I bow to you, my queen."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:25.671
That's cool!
-Yes. Yes, it is.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.374
And it's gonna be even cooler
when he put me in the next one.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.942
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.011
-You think you're gonna be
in the next one.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.545
But you told him
exactly what you want to be.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.548
-Oh, I better be
in the next one!

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.516
I live-tweeted for four hours!

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:40.286
I better damn well
be the star of the next one!

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.822
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.358
-I -- I think you'd be great.
I think you'd be --

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.493
What are the conditions?
What do you want to play?

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.963
A hero or villain?
-I want to be a villain.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:54.133
I want to be a villain, and I
want to be the worst villain.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.268
I want to be the villain
that people be like,

00:03:56.268 --> 00:04:01.373
"Somebody kill this bitch!"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:04.710
[ Laughter ]
-You have to do this.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.545
When we talked about it before,
you said you --

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:10.349
I think you would be great
in an action movie or TV show.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.484
-I mean, my knees ain't good,
but, you know,

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.420
as long as we get
a stunt double, we good.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.456
-[ Laughs ]
Wait.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.957
So you're like,
"stop, stop, wait, stop!

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.158
All right, let me get
in the car, hold on.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.292
Slow down."
-"Stop, stop!

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:21.827
Hold on, hold on.
Let the knee girl come in.

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:24.363
Let the knee girl come in."
-Oh, my God.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.833
I really do believe that you
would be great, by the way.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.867
I want to talk to you
about this weekend.

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:31.870
I can't think of anyone better
to host the MTV

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:37.276
movie and TV awards this Sunday.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.979
You must be excited to get in
front of a crowd again, right?

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.114
And it's live?
-Oh, Jimmy. Okay.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.983
So, you know I've been going up

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.885
so I can get ready
for the monologue.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.887
And, Jimmy, I'mma tell you,
the first time I was in front

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.888
of an audience --
The last time I was in front

00:04:49.888 --> 00:04:52.992
of a live audience
was when I taped "Time Machine,"

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:57.063
2019, September the 10th.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.198
-And that's the last time
I was on stage.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.167
And when I got on stage,
I'm not gonna lie,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.736
I got a little emotional.
It was, uh...

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:06.338
-Yeah.
-It was very therapeutic.

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:09.241
And I didn't know that that
was the thing I was missing.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:12.845
-Yeah, it's wild.
Nothing like a live audience.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.013
We have a beautiful --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:16.715
-There's nothing like it.
There's nothing like it.

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:19.451
Nothing like it.
Nothing like it.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:21.954
And, Jimmy, I can't wait,

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.490
because this is gonna be
the coming-out party.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.960
Like, we've been locked up
for almost a year and a half.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.364
I'm about to make this
a party, party, party.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.066
Okay?
I'm talking about --

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:36.669
It's gonna be fun.
Oh, my God, Jimmy.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.938
It's gonna be so funny, Jimmy!

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.606
Jimmy, it's gonna be so funny.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.274
-All right, I believe it!
I believe you!

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:44.610
Is there any celebrities
that are gonna be there

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.911
that you're gonna be
excited to meet?

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:48.013
-Well, I'm gonna be there.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:50.249
-That's all that matters.
That's the only rea--

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.318
I will be watching.
That's all I want.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:55.321
Leslie Jones,
the MTV Movie and TV Awards

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.757
airs this Sunday at 9:00 p.m.

